<Layout title="Terms · Dipity" description="The terms for using Dipity.">
  <article class="prose mx-auto px-5 pt-10 sm:px-8">
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      These terms cover your use of the Dipity app, made by Coracle Social LLC ("Coracle", "we").
      By using Dipity you agree to them. If you don't agree, please don't use the app.
    </p>
    <p><strong>Effective October 7, 2026.</strong></p>

    <h2>What Dipity is</h2>
    <p>
      Dipity is an app that exchanges posts directly with other phones nearby. Coracle runs no
      service for it, and does not host, receive, review or store anything that people post.
    </p>

    <h2>Your content</h2>
    <p>
      What you post is yours, and you are responsible for it. Your phone hands each post to the
      phones your settings allow. The people who receive a post can keep and copy it, so you cannot
      fully withdraw a post once it has been shared.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>You may not use Dipity to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>break the law, or encourage anyone else to;</li>
      <li>harass, threaten, impersonate or stalk anyone;</li>
      <li>
        share content that exploits or endangers children, as our <a href="/child-safety"
          >child safety standards</a
        > describe;
      </li>
      <li>share nudity, sexual content or graphic violence;</li>
      <li>share other people's private information without their permission;</li>
      <li>flood your neighbours with spam, or interfere with other people's phones.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Coracle cannot remove content from anyone's phone or suspend anyone's account. Instead, you
      can flag posts, mute, block or suppress anyone, and choose whose posts your phone accepts.
      You can also report a post to us from its flag dialog.
    </p>

    <h2>Your key</h2>
    <p>
      Your identity is a key stored on your phone. Nobody, including Coracle, can recover the key if
      you lose it, or revoke it if someone steals it. You are responsible for keeping it safe and
      for backing it up.
    </p>

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      Dipity is provided as is, without warranties of any kind. We don't promise that it will always
      work, that posts will reach anyone in particular, or that it will be free of errors.
    </p>

    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent the law allows, Coracle is not liable for any indirect, incidental or
      consequential damages, or for any loss of data, arising from your use of Dipity or from content
      other people share through it.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms. When we do, we'll post the new version here and change the date
      above. If you continue to use Dipity after a change, you accept the new terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Send questions about these terms to <a href="mailto:support@coracle.social"
        >support@coracle.social</a
      >.
    </p>
